=== file: README.md ===
# Weekly release newsletter workflow

This project contains a confidential-data-aware drafting and editor-review workflow. It stops on unclear decisions and bounds revisions to three rounds. An editor's typed `approve` decision gates the workflow's approved-draft result.

## Integration boundary

The script declares the planned release-notes source, cursor, and webhook integrations. Their deployment configuration and contracts are not supplied by the plan, so this workflow intentionally does not invoke them: it accepts already-filtered release notes as input, does not read or advance a cursor, and does not post. In particular, the generic webhook declaration does not implement or guarantee the plan's stable idempotency-key contract.

Before enabling the planned Monday schedule or any posting, deployment must provide audited integrations for fetching notes newer than the last successfully posted cursor, persisting the cursor only after confirmed posting, and sending with a stable idempotency key. Keep the sender separate from the agent that reads release-note text; pass it only approved, typed values. Require approval for sends and cursor writes. Unknown outcomes must stop for operator review.

The plan leaves the organization-approved provider and model configuration to deployment. The script uses the plan-listed model identifier `gpt-6-luna`; confirm that it is available and approved in the target environment before running.

## Run and test

Run the workflow with `release_notes_payload` containing only notes newer than the saved cursor. Pass `NO_NEW_NOTES` when there are no new notes. Review and approval are interactive; an unclear response is not approval.

Run the logic tests with:

```text
weave test main.loom
``` 
